@NODE "intro" "MorphUAE - Introduction"
@PREV "main"
@NEXT "req"

 @{b}@{u}Introduction@{uu}@{ub}
 
 MorphUAE is an enhanced variant of the emulator E-UAE specially made for MorphOS.

 You might think to yourself, isn't there allready a port of E-UAE for MorphOS ?
 And the answer to that is ofcourse yes, however the version ported done by Fabien Coeurjoly was last updated
 more than 10 years ago.

 E-UAE is very Un*x-like in it's configuration handling which only consist of textfiles.
 It also lack MUI-support so it's purely a Intuition window.

 And that was the key idea of the birth of MorphUAE. Add a better and easier user experince with some new features.

@ENDNODE

@NODE "req" "MorphUAE - Requirements"
@PREV "intro"
@NEXT "install"

 @{b}@{u}Requirements@{uu}@{ub}

 This program needs following to run :

 · MorphOS 3.x or higher
 · TrueColour / 24Bit graphics
 · Amiga Kickstart ROMs (for best compability)

@ENDNODE

@NODE "install" "MorphUAE - Installation"
@PREV "req"
@NEXT "usage"

 @{b}@{u}Installation@{uu}@{ub}

 This program doesn't need any installation and because of that doesn't come with
 any form of installer script. Just place it where you want and run it from there! =)

 Place your Amiga Kickstart files in the folder named @{b}Kickstarts@{ub}
 The default name which the emulator uses for the name here is

 @{b}Kick1.rom@{ub} : OCS based hardware
 @{b}Kick2.rom@{ub} : ECS based hardware
 @{b}Kick3.rom@{ub} : AGA based hardware
 @{b}rom.key@{ub}   : Your AmigaForever/Cloanto keyfile (if you have encrypted ROM files that is)

 However the name can be anything and can be adjusted in the settings window on each machine type.
 Naming the files as in the list above should get you a running emulator directly withouth any changes.

 MorphUAE comes bundled with AROS m68k ROM images which is used incase there is no real Amiga Kickstarts found.
 This is a re-implementaion of the official Kickstart for m68k Amigas. It's not perfect but should work "good enough" in most cases.
 For best compability it's always best to try to use a real Amiga Kickstart ROM.

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage" "MorphUAE - Usage"
@PREV "install"
@NEXT "faq"

 @{b}@{u}Usage@{uu}@{ub}

 This program's user interface consists of a couple of fields/elements,
 which are briefly explained below...

  @{" Main Window  " LINK "usage-main"     }
  @{" Settings     " LINK "usage-settings" }
  @{" CLI / Shell  " LINK "usage-shell"    }
  @{" Ambient      " LINK "usage-ambient"  }
  @{" Hotkeys      " LINK "usage-hotkeys"  }
  @{" ARexx        " LINK "usage-arexx"    }

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-main" "MorphUAE - Main Window"
@PREV "usage"
@NEXT "usage-settings"

 @{b}· Main window :@{ub}

   The first thing you see when you start the emulator is the main window.
   This window consist mostly of a render area for the emulated graphics and below that you have a toolbar.


 @{b}· Toolbar :@{ub}
   
   From this toolbar you can adjust the emulator settings and control the behaviour of it.
   The toolbar consist of number of clickable symbols which are described below.


    @{b}· Settings :@{ub}

      This button will open the settings window where you can adjust the different setups on


    @{b}· Reset :@{ub}

      This button will reset the emulator in either an Soft or Hard reset (depending on what you have selected
      in the settings window on the General tab).


    @{b}· Fullscreen :@{ub}

      By pressing this button the emulator opens up a fullscreen window and scale the graphics to fit the full screen.
      It will remove the toolbar and only show the render data on the window. If you want to revert back to window mode
      please use the hotkey combination


    @{b}· Screenshot :@{ub}

      By pressing this button you will get a screenshot of what is currently rendered in the main window.
      The saved image will be stored in @{b}RAM:@{ub} named @{b}MorphUAE-Screenshoot.png@{ub}


    @{b}· Pause/Resume :@{ub}

      This button will Pause or Resume emulation depending on what current state is.
      An paused emulation is identified by that the window title is change to @{b}MorphUAE - Paused@{ub}


    @{b}· About :@{ub}

      This button will open the About window...


    @{b}· Joystick port 0 & 1 Selector:@{ub}

      Here you can change the emulated joystick port during the runtime of the emulation.
      See it like you virtually swapping out the mouse with a joystick or vice versa.


    @{b}· Eject Disk Images :@{ub}

      Pressing this will eject all previously added/mounted disk images in DF0-DF3


    @{b}· Disk Images / LED indicators :@{ub}
    
      Theese buttons represents the disk images and will indicate read/write operations when it's active.
      They are enumerated from left to right : DF0, DF1, DF2, DF3.
      Pressing them will open up an ASL-requester where you can select the .ADF-file you want to mount/use on the emulator.

      If you drag'n'drop an ADF-file to the main window, DF0 will add and mount that file to it's container.
      This can be done if you quickly want to swap disks.

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-settings" "MorphUAE - Settings"
@PREV "usage-main"
@NEXT "usage-shell"

 @{b}Settings :@{ub}

   This window consist of a number of tabs which you can configure General settings for the emulator or specific ones
   related to the machine type.
   
   All of the configurable tabs have a "Reset to Default" button if you want to get back to originat state of the settings.

    @{b}· General tab :@{ub}

      The @{b}Machine Type@{ub} button let you select which of the tabs that shall be the default emulated machine when it start up.
      Each of the selected tabs have options to select Kickstart ROM and other machine specific parameters.
      This selection can be overrided by using CLI/Shell flags if needed.

     @{b} Sound section@{ub} will let you configure the output quality of the emulated sound or even disable it completely.

     @{b} I/O Devices@{ub} Lets you select which type of emulated device that shall be connected to the Mouse/Joystick port
      Here you can also set the emulated floppy drive speed. Some games/demos might have issues with faster
      speed higher than normal hence this might be a good thing to try if issues would occure.

     @{b} Graphics section@{ub} Here you can alter how precise the emulated graphics shall be presented.
      If your machine struggles with graphics intensive parts that result in choppy sound or general slugginess, this might
      be a good "playground" to change it for a better result.



    @{b}· OCS tab :@{ub}
     This machine type is intended to emulate the first generations of Amiga with OCS chipset, lower memory fotprint and Kickstart 1.x ROM.
     Typical machine here is A500/A1000/A2000 (MC68000)


    @{b}· ECS tab :@{ub}
     This machine type is very similar to the OCS settings but configuration is using the ECS chipset (which where you can select
     if you want ECS Agnus, Denise or both emulated. Kickstart 2.x ROM, typical machine A500+/A600 (MC68000).


    @{b}· AGA tab :@{ub}
    This is the last generation of Amigas using AGA chipset and default 2Mb CHIP RAM with optional 1-8 Mb FAST RAM. Kickstart 3.x ROM
    Typical machine A1200. (MC68020)


    @{b}· Custom tab :@{ub}

    In this machine type you can pretty much customize your emulated machine to be what ever you like.
    You can add up to 2 virtual harddisks (a path to your host OS where files can be easily copied from and to).
    Device and Volume name will be used in the emulated environment.
    You can select which emulated CPU is going to be used (68020, 68040 or 68060).
    There is also an option to turn of PPC JIT Compiler with different amount of caches, this option can cause issues during emulation but also
    boost emulation speeds a huge bit, This is very much depended of what type of binaries/software that is used during the emulation.
    

   @{b}· About tab :@{ub}

   Here you can see the software version/revision and credits.


   @{b}·Use, Save or Cancel buttons :@{ub}

     @{b}Use@{ub} button will store all settings in ENV: and restart the emulator with the new settings...

     @{b}Save & Use@{ub} button stores all settings in both ENV and ENVARC and restart the emulator with the new settings.

     @{b}Save@{ub} button stores the settings to ENVARC: and uses it next reboot of the system

     @{b}Cancel@{ub} button just closes the settings window


@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-shell" "MorphUAE - CLI / Shell"
@PREV "usage-settings"
@NEXT "usage-ambient"

 @{b}CLI/Shell :@{ub}

    @{b}-ocs@{ub} : Will override the default settings and use what is setup under the @{b}OCS tab@{ub} in the settings window.
    @{b}-ecs@{ub} : Will override the default settings and use what is setup under the @{b}ECS tab@{ub} in the settings window.
    @{b}-aga@{ub} : Will override the default settings and use what is setup under the @{b}AGA tab@{ub} in the settings window.
    @{b}-custom@{ub} : Will override the default settings and use what is setup under the @{b}Custom tab@{ub} in the settings window.
    @{b}-nochecksum@{ub} : This will ignore the checksum control of the Kickstart/ROM file, some homebrew ROM's doesn't work otherwise like diagnostic ROMs.
    @{b}-fullscreen@{ub} : This will start the emulator in fullscreen mode.

    @{b}-0 <ADF file>@{ub} : Insert an ADF disk image on DF0: at startup.
    @{b}-1 <ADF file>@{ub} : Insert an ADF disk image on DF1: at startup.

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-ambient" "MorphUAE - Ambient"
@PREV "usage-shell"
@NEXT "usage-hotkeys"

 @{b}Ambient :@{ub}

   If you want to automatically start and load an ADF disk image in Ambient on MorphOS you can go to the Settings menu in Ambient.

   Settings
      |
      +- Ambient...

   In the settings, locate the "Mime" option in the left panel.
   Search for 'adf' when you see the x-adf type double click on this.

   · Add a new event type, name it something suitable.
   · Change the type to @{b}AmigaDOS@{ub}
   · Set the event type to : DoubleClick
   · Check the option "Change working directory to destination"
   
   · Add following string to the field : @{b}run >NIL: Work:Emulators/MorphUAE/MorphUAE -0 %sp@{ub}
     The above string you will have to change to the location where you have MorphUAE located, this is just an example.

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-hotkeys" "MorphUAE - Hotkeys"
@PREV "usage-ambient"
@NEXT "usage-arexx"

 There are hotkeys associated to the toolbar in the main window and 

 @{b}· Toolbar hotkeys :@{ub}

    · Reset : @{b}ctrl+lalt+r@{ub}
    · Fullscreen/Window toggle : @{b}lalt+enter@{ub}
    · Screenshoot : @{b}ctrl+lalt+s@{ub}
    · Pause/Resume : @{b}ctrl+lalt+p@{ub}
    · Eject Disk Images : @{b}ctrl+lalt+e@{ub}
    · Insert DF0 Image : @{b}ctrl+lalt+1@{ub}
    · Insert DF1 Image : @{b}ctrl+lalt+2@{ub}
    · Insert DF2 Image : @{b}ctrl+lalt+3@{ub}
    · Insert DF3 Image : @{b}ctrl+lalt+4@{ub}

 @{b}· Other hotkeys :@{ub}

    · Toggle the toolbar on / off : @{b}ctrl+lalt+t@{ub}
    · Quit the emulator : @{b}ctrl+lalt+q@{ub}

@ENDNODE

@NODE "usage-arexx" "MorphUAE - ARexx"
