@NODE "faq" "MorphUAE - FAQ"
@PREV "usageprefs"
@NEXT "news"

@{b}@{u}FAQ - Frequently Asked Questions@{uu}@{ub}

* @{b}Q = Question@{ub}
* @{b}A = Answer@{ub}

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Q - Where can I find Amiga ROM files ?

A - Easiest way is to buy a licence from www.amigaforever.com
    The cheapest way is to obtain them for Android (via Google Play) :
    https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.cloanto.amigaforever.essentials

    If you allready have a real Amiga you can dump the content of the kickstart
    directly from that and use it in the emulator. There are several tools on
    Aminet for this purpose.


Q - The render window does not have the correct colours and the graphics looks strange ?

A - This emulator NEEDS 24bit resolution to be able to work as intended.


Q - The mouse position on the Amiga (emulation) side is not fully in sync with the
    host mouse coordinations ?

A - This issue needs to be adressed in future versions of MorphUAE and it's a
    well known issue.


Q - When using the fullscreen mode the graphics is not as "big" as expected, how come ?

A - Add a 24/32 bit screenmode with the resolution 640 x 512 pixels in the monitor
    preferences and the screen should fill it up better.


Q - Can I use P96 driver for RTG software with MorphUAE ?

A - No, not at this point.
    The main idea behind this emulator is to have compability with games & demos
    back from the Amiga days. Apart from that, system friendly RTG programs runs
    straight into MorphOS directly so there is nothing really to gain with adding
    this into the emulator. Maybe one day but it's not at all on the prio list.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


@ENDNODE

